# Drupal 11 / PHP 8.5 Standards

Target: Drupal 11 APIs only — no deprecated approaches. PHP 8.5 features (typed properties, enums, readonly, first-class callables) are welcome where they clarify code.

## Coding standards
- Drupal coding standards (PSR-12 based): 2-space indent, docblocks on all classes and public methods, `declare(strict_types=1)` in new class files.
- `CamelCase` classes, `lowerCamelCase` properties/methods, `snake_case` procedural functions and hooks (`mymodule_entity_presave()`).
- Custom modules in `web/modules/custom/`, custom themes in `web/themes/custom/`; PHP classes under the module's `src/` with PSR-4 namespaces.

## Architecture
- Prefer classes (services, controllers, plugins, event subscribers) over procedural code; `.module` files only hold hooks that have no OO replacement.
- Inject services via the container (constructor injection, `create()` factory); never call `\Drupal::service()` inside injectable classes.
- Use core APIs instead of reinventing: Entity API for data (never raw SQL against entity tables), Form API with validate/submit handlers, Config API for settings, Queue API / cron for background work, Batch API for long-running operations.

## Database and updates
- Database API with parameterized queries or entity queries — never string-concatenated SQL.
- Schema changes only through `hook_update_N()`; keep data migrations separate from schema updates.
- Never hack core or contrib — extend via modules, patches go through composer-patches.

## Caching and performance
- Attach cache metadata (`#cache` contexts, tags, max-age) to render arrays; invalidate via cache tags, don't disable caching.
- Load entities in bulk (`loadMultiple()`, entity queries) — no loads inside loops.

## Theming
- Logic in preprocess functions, not Twig; templates only render prepared variables.
- Attach assets via `*.libraries.yml` and `#attached` — no hardcoded `<script>`/`<link>` tags.
- Prefer Single Directory Components (SDC) for new theme components.

## Security
- Sanitize output: Twig auto-escaping, `Xss::filter()`, `Html::escape()`; never render raw user input.
- Check permissions before protected actions (`hasPermission()`, `AccessResult::allowedIf()`); deny by default.
- Config export stays deterministic: no `uuid`/`_core` churn in committed config diffs.
